  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "This lineup needs to find its footing against elite arms.",
    "what_this_means": "The Athletics trailed by three before they scraped together four runs in the sixth and held on. That is a survival story dressed as a win, and it exposed something fragile about how they're winning right now. They converted five of eleven RISP situations, which matters. Scoring is hard. But the game never felt in control. J.T. Ginn gave them six solid innings, and Brady Basso and Elvis Alvarado closed it out clean, but that bullpen work only mattered because the offense finally woke up late. This is not a team firing on all cylinders. This is a team that sneaks wins from behind because it has learned to sit in ugly games and wait. That math gets harder every time they do it.",
